## Summary

Replaced the site's build-time image-optimization plugin (`next-export-optimize-images`, capped at Next 14/15) with `next-image-export-optimizer` (supports Next 16), unblocking the future Next major bump without touching Fumadocs/Next versions in this ticket.

- `next.config.mjs`: dropped the `withExportImages()` wrapper; added `images.loader: 'custom'`, `transpilePackages`, and an `env` block configuring quality 75, WebP output, and an `_optimized`-style output directory (matching the old `export-images.config.js` behavior, which is now deleted).
- Swapped all image call sites (`layout.config.tsx`, `page.client.tsx`, `image-zoom.tsx`) from `Image`/`Picture` to the new `ExportedImage` component.
- `image-zoom.tsx`'s lightbox no longer computes an explicit optimized `src` (the old plugin's `getOptimizedImageProps` has no equivalent) — verified via the library's source that it now correctly falls back to cloning the already-optimized `<ExportedImage>` DOM node, so there's no regression.
